# Simplicity First

- Implement only what was requested; avoid speculative features.
- Avoid single-use abstractions and unrequested configurability.
- Do not add error handling for impossible scenarios.
- Prefer the minimum code that solves the task.
- If the solution feels overengineered, simplify before finalizing.
